WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.408 --> 00:00:13.390
Long ago in Baghdad, lived a merchant named Ali.

2
00:00:15.931 --> 00:00:19.113
As a good Muslim, he decided to make a pilgrimage to Mecca.

3
00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:26.257
Knowing this journey would take a long time, he sold all of his belongings and rented out his

4
00:00:26.277 --> 00:00:32.140
house. His life savings of a thousand gold coins was too heavy to travel with.

5
00:00:34.176 --> 00:00:37.857
So he placed the coins in a large jar and covered them with olives.

6
00:00:39.597 --> 00:00:43.459
After sealing the jar, he took it to a neighbor, who was also a merchant.

7
00:00:43.479 --> 00:00:48.220
"My friend, I will leave for Mecca tomorrow.

8
00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:51.101
May I store these olives with you until I return?"

9
00:00:53.321 --> 00:00:56.602
The merchant, whose name was Mahid, handed Ali a key.

10
00:00:56.622 --> 00:01:00.483
"Put your jar anywhere in my warehouse.

11
00:01:01.103 --> 00:01:03.884
It will be safe and untouched until you return."

12
00:01:05.532 --> 00:01:08.253
Ali's journey took much longer than he had expected.

13
00:01:09.793 --> 00:01:13.614
After Mecca he traveled further, exploring the wonders of the region.

14
00:01:15.335 --> 00:01:17.415
Soon seven years had passed.

15
00:01:19.956 --> 00:01:23.497
Mahid had forgotten all about Ali until one evening over dinner.

16
00:01:23.517 --> 00:01:28.438
"How delicious some olives would be," Mahid's wife remarked.

17
00:01:28.458 --> 00:01:30.959
"Actually, we have some.

18
00:01:31.619 --> 00:01:33.540
Remember the jar Ali left with us?

19
00:01:34.304 --> 00:01:37.306
He has been gone so long that I doubt he will ever come back.

20
00:01:38.007 --> 00:01:40.248
I will check to see if the olives are still edible."

21
00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:44.531
"Olives cannot keep for seven years.

22
00:01:45.172 --> 00:01:47.834
Besides, you shouldn't break your promise to Ali."

23
00:01:48.854 --> 00:01:50.295
Mahid gave in for the moment.

24
00:01:51.136 --> 00:01:55.359
But later that evening, while his wife was asleep, he sneaked into the warehouse.

25
00:01:59.602 --> 00:02:02.604
Opening the jar, he saw that the olives at the top were moldy.

26
00:02:05.008 --> 00:02:07.170
But then something shiny caught his eye.

27
00:02:11.392 --> 00:02:12.513
he greedily whispered.

28
00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:19.256
The next day he emptied the jar of the gold, filled it with fresh olives, and resealed it.

29
00:02:21.377 --> 00:02:24.839
Ali returned the following month and retrieved his jar from Mahid.

30
00:02:28.281 --> 00:02:30.442
To his dismay, he found no gold.

31
00:02:31.803 --> 00:02:33.224
He angrily went to Mahid.

32
00:02:34.132 --> 00:02:36.473
Mahid, however, denied stealing the gold.

33
00:02:36.493 --> 00:02:39.654
"You placed the jar in my warehouse yourself.

34
00:02:40.494 --> 00:02:42.834
You retrieved it, and it was still sealed.

35
00:02:43.275 --> 00:02:45.515
How dare you say I've committed a crime!"

36
00:02:49.056 --> 00:02:51.377
Ali decided to take his complaint to a judge.

37
00:02:53.137 --> 00:02:56.558
Not knowing how to resolve the dispute, the judge sent Ali away.

38
00:03:00.879 --> 00:03:02.800
Ali was determined to get his gold back.

39
00:03:03.808 --> 00:03:07.591
He wrote to the caliph, the ruler of Baghdad, who agreed to hear the case.

40
00:03:10.252 --> 00:03:14.635
Meanwhile, news of Ali and Mahid's dispute had spread throughout Baghdad.

41
00:03:16.076 --> 00:03:18.598
The caliph was angry that the judge had done nothing.

42
00:03:20.279 --> 00:03:22.481
But the caliph too was puzzled by the evidence.

43
00:03:24.802 --> 00:03:28.545
The night before the hearing, the caliph and his advisor walked through the city.

44
00:03:30.106 --> 00:03:33.308
They soon came upon some children acting out a courtroom scene.

45
00:03:35.768 --> 00:03:37.449
One boy pretended to be the caliph.

46
00:03:38.509 --> 00:03:40.010
"Bring me the olives!"

47
00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:43.311
he demanded to another boy, who was pretending to be Ali.

48
00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:49.874
The pretend Ali placed an invisible jar before the pretend caliph.

49
00:03:50.914 --> 00:03:53.195
The child caliph pretended to eat an olive.

50
00:03:53.215 --> 00:03:58.317
"Delicious. But olives cannot keep for seven years.

51
00:03:59.378 --> 00:04:02.899
Summon an olive merchant to give testimony on this matter!"

52
00:04:03.339 --> 00:04:04.640
the pretend caliph ordered.

53
00:04:06.544 --> 00:04:09.627
At this, the real caliph realized the answer he had been seeking.

54
00:04:09.647 --> 00:04:12.390
"Bring this boy to me tomorrow.

55
00:04:13.711 --> 00:04:18.756
And remind the real Ali to bring his jar of olives," he whispered to his advisor.

56
00:04:18.776 --> 00:04:21.339
"Bring an olive merchant as well."

57
00:04:23.601 --> 00:04:26.384
The next day Ali and Mahid stood before the caliph.

58
00:04:28.826 --> 00:04:30.388
The child caliph was nearby.

59
00:04:32.236 --> 00:04:37.679
"Today this child shall hear your case and give you a fair verdict," the caliph said.

60
00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:43.182
Ali and Mahid both pleaded their case to the child, who seemed uninterested.

61
00:04:45.123 --> 00:04:47.064
Then the child called the olive merchant.

62
00:04:50.086 --> 00:04:52.627
"Taste an olive," the child instructed.

63
00:04:53.728 --> 00:04:57.150
The olive merchant was irritated at being given orders by a child.

64
00:04:57.870 --> 00:05:00.372
He looked to the real caliph, who nodded approvingly.

65
00:05:03.688 --> 00:05:05.609
And so the merchant tasted an olive.

66
00:05:05.629 --> 00:05:10.110
"Does it taste like a seven-year-old olive?"

67
00:05:10.470 --> 00:05:11.310
the child asked.

68
00:05:12.670 --> 00:05:18.032
"No. Olives lose their color and turn rotten after three years," the merchant replied.

69
00:05:18.052 --> 00:05:20.413
"These olives are fresh."

70
00:05:22.153 --> 00:05:23.553
The boy pointed at Mahid.

71
00:05:24.194 --> 00:05:25.934
"You are lying, sir.

72
00:05:26.454 --> 00:05:30.415
These olives are new, and you have stolen Ali's gold."

73
00:05:32.176 --> 00:05:35.441
Mahid panicked, for he knew the punishment for thieves was harsh.

74
00:05:36.681 --> 00:05:39.683
Then he confessed and begged for mercy from the real caliph.

75
00:05:41.163 --> 00:05:44.105
The caliph ordered Mahid to give back Ali's gold.

76
00:05:45.465 --> 00:05:50.587
Then he rewarded the child with a hundred gold coins and sent him to replace the useless judge.
